WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.846
Welcome to my home.

2
00:00:08.847 --> 00:00:16.944
I live here in this little nest inside this large clock, which is here in this tall clock tower in the great city of London.

3
00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:19.230
I'm a Big Ben bird.

4
00:00:19.231 --> 00:00:24.933
Big Ben is in the Palace of Westminster, which is the main government building in Britain.

5
00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:30.242
This is where the most important decisions in the United Kingdom are made.

6
00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:33.437
It is also where the prime minister works.

7
00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:39.304
The clock tower is 97 meters tall, and it has a very unusual clock.

8
00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:44.113
Most clocks have only one face, but this clock has four faces.

9
00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:46.503
Each one looks in a different direction.

10
00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:51.302
That way, people from all around London can look up and see what time it is.

11
00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:57.616
The clock does not need a battery or electricity like your clocks at home.

12
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:01.547
This is an old-fashioned clock. It runs on weights.

13
00:01:01.548 --> 00:01:07.788
Increasing the weights slows the clock a tiny bit, while reducing the weights speeds it up a little.

14
00:01:07.789 --> 00:01:10.695
If the clock is not keeping perfect time,

15
00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:19.899
the clock master adds or removes one penny at a time until the weight is just right, and the clock keeps perfect time again.

16
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.450
The clock master still uses the same old-fashioned pennies from when the clock was built.

17
00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:30.123
I often hear people say, "Look over there. It's Big Ben."

18
00:01:30.124 --> 00:01:33.701
Most people think that Big Ben is the name of this tower.

19
00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:37.966
But did you know that Big Ben is not the name of the clock tower?

20
00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:43.765
It's the name of the biggest and most famous bell inside the tower.

21
00:01:43.766 --> 00:01:47.432
The tower itself is called St. Stephen's Tower.

22
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:52.921
Big Ben rings every hour of the day so that people can hear what time it is.

23
00:01:52.922 --> 00:01:57.647
A hammer strikes the great bell the same number of times as the hour.

24
00:01:57.648 --> 00:02:03.550
So if you count the number of times Big Ben rings, you'll know what time it is.

25
00:02:03.551 --> 00:02:07.465
There are other smaller bells in the tower as well.

26
00:02:07.466 --> 00:02:12.688
These play a short melody every 15 minutes to signal the quarter hours.

27
00:02:12.689 --> 00:02:15.876
Big Ben is one of the biggest bells in the world.

28
00:02:15.877 --> 00:02:19.749
It is much taller than even a really tall man.

29
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:26.893
Big Ben is 2.8 meters high, and it weighs 13,760 kilograms.

30
00:02:26.894 --> 00:02:30.995
That is more than the weight of 175 men.

31
00:02:30.996 --> 00:02:38.232
It was made on Saturday, April 10, 1858, and was named after Sir Benjamin Hall.

32
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:46.499
Benjamin, or Ben for short, was a very large man who was in charge of buying the new bell for the St. Stephen's Tower clock.

33
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:51.406
One of the most amazing things about Big Ben is the place where it was made.

34
00:02:51.407 --> 00:02:57.455
Big Ben comes from the Whitechapel Bell Foundry here in London.

35
00:02:57.456 --> 00:03:03.974
The Whitechapel Bell Foundry is famous because many of the great bells in the world were made here.

36
00:03:03.975 --> 00:03:09.357
But it is also famous because this factory is over four hundred years old.

37
00:03:09.358 --> 00:03:15.962
The Whitechapel Bell Foundry began in 1570 and is still in business today.

38
00:03:15.963 --> 00:03:20.889
It is the oldest company in Britain and one of the oldest companies in the world.

39
00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:27.335
Since the opening of the Whitechapel Bell Foundry, there have been over 27 kings and queens in Britain.

40
00:03:27.336 --> 00:03:33.327
Some of them, like King George V and Queen Mary, even visited this factory.

41
00:03:33.328 --> 00:03:37.441
The factory has always been on this same street.

42
00:03:37.442 --> 00:03:43.392
In 1670, during the Great Fire of London, the Whitechapel Bell Foundry burned down.

43
00:03:43.393 --> 00:03:48.495
But right after the fire, the owners rebuilt their factory just across the street.

44
00:03:48.496 --> 00:03:53.075
And that is where it still stands today.

45
00:03:53.076 --> 00:03:59.461
The most famous bells that were made at the Whitechapel Bell Foundry are the Liberty Bell in the United States,

46
00:03:59.462 --> 00:04:04.456
the Great Bell of Montreal Cathedral in Canada, and of course, Big Ben.

47
00:04:04.457 --> 00:04:11.217
But now there are some new, very special bells that are being made at the factory.

48
00:04:11.218 --> 00:04:13.624
They are called the Bells of September.

49
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:20.932
Three large bells are being made to remember the very sad day when the World Trade Center in New York City was destroyed.

50
00:04:20.933 --> 00:04:23.284
The first one has just been finished.

51
00:04:23.285 --> 00:04:28.617
It was made to look exactly like the Liberty Bell.

52
00:04:28.618 --> 00:04:30.826
Listen! Can you hear that?

53
00:04:30.827 --> 00:04:34.778
It's Big Ben ringing, so it must be twelve o'clock.

54
00:04:34.779 --> 00:04:41.727
I should hurry back to the bell tower now and get my lunch.
